diff --git a/docs/file-drag-preview.md b/docs/file-drag-preview.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..75c070f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/file-drag-preview.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# File drag preview
+
+This preview adds the `file_transfer` capability to the existing authenticated
+v6 connection. Peers without that capability retain the existing crossing
+behavior. The source stages the complete selection on the peer before it
+crosses the pointer and requests a native drag. A release before the handoff
+cancels the pending transfer. The implementation supports up to 32 regular
+files with at most 10 GiB in total; directories and symbolic links are not
+supported.
+
+`drag_begin` identifies a random 128-bit drag ID and file count. After the
+peer acknowledges it, each file uses `file_offer`, `file_chunk`, and
+`file_finish`, with a separate random 128-bit file ID, sequential offsets,
+at most 32 KiB per chunk, and a SHA-256 digest. Each step is acknowledged;
+this bounds buffering. File names are single portable names rather than paths.
+`drag_ready` is acknowledged after all files arrive, and `drag_start` asks the
+target to begin its platform drag only after the source has handed over input.
+`drag_cancel` and `file_cancel` end the corresponding pending operation.
+
+Received bytes are staged in a temporary directory. A verified file is
+published there without overwriting an existing entry. Cancelled or incomplete
+transfers are removed. Successfully dropped staging files are retained because
+the destination application may copy them asynchronously after the drag loop
+returns. No assumption is made that this indicates the copy has completed.
+
+The native Finder and Windows Explorer integration must be tested on actual
+macOS and Windows desktops before this preview is treated as a release.
